    <string name="plan_format_title">Plan format</string>
    <string name="plan_format_text">A plan is a list of phases; each phase says how many weeks its days repeat, and each day lists its exercises. Sets are plain text (\"4 x 8\", \"3 x 30 s\", \"3 rounds\"). If your plan has no phases, just write the days and it\'ll be treated as a single phase.</string>
    <string name="plan_copy_example">Copy example</string>
    <string name="plan_format_example_markdown"># My strength plan\nThree days a week for eight weeks.\n\n## Base (4 weeks)\nLearn the movement with a comfortable weight.\nProgression: add weight when all 10 reps feel easy.\n\n### Monday — Push\nWarm-up: 6 min bike + shoulder mobility\n- Bench press — 4 x 8\n- Shoulder press — 3 x 10 (don\'t lock your elbows)\n- Plank — 3 x 30 s\n\n### Thursday — Pull\n- Lat pulldown — 4 x 10\n- Seated row — 4 x 10\n\n## Load (4 weeks)\n\n### Monday — Strength\n- Squat — 5 x 5\n- Bench press — 5 x 5</string>
    <string name="plan_format_example_json">{\n  \"name\": \"My strength plan\",\n  \"description\": \"Three days a week, 8 weeks.\",\n  \"phases\": [\n    {\n      \"name\": \"Base\",\n      \"weeks\": 4,\n      \"description\": \"Learn the movement with a comfortable weight.\",\n      \"progression\": \"Add weight when all 10 reps feel easy.\",\n      \"days\": [\n        {\n          \"weekday\": \"Monday\",\n          \"title\": \"Push\",\n          \"warmup\": \"6 min bike + shoulder mobility\",\n          \"exercises\": [\n            { \"name\": \"Bench press\", \"scheme\": \"4 x 8\" },\n            { \"name\": \"Shoulder press\", \"scheme\": \"3 x 10\", \"note\": \"Don\'t lock your elbows\" },\n            { \"name\": \"Plank\", \"scheme\": \"3 x 30 s\" }\n          ]\n        }\n      ]\n    }\n  ]\n}</string>
